  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "All four aggregation×fusion combinations for the top architecture (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile) have been tested, with config_006 (transformer, weighted) as the clear best at 0.725. The evidence strongly indicates scgpt (~0.52) and pca_n2000 (~0.59) are inferior RNA encoders, and resnet50 underperforms imagenet_vit_l (0.688 vs 0.721 for the same aggregation/fusion). Config_038 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) is the closest untested variant to the current best, differing only in image encoder. It tests whether the transformer+weighted fusion advantage is robust to a weaker image encoder, confirming the architecture ranking. I expect accuracy around 0.69–0.70, unlikely to beat config_006, but it is the most informative remaining test given the near-exhausted promising space. Expected cost is ~5 GPU hours (similar to config_011 at 5.16), making it moderately expensive but justified as the final confirmation before the last experiment slot."
}

